  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This intervention aims to strengthen the institutional capacity of employers&#x2019; organizations in Afghanistan to become strong, representative, and effective actors in promoting decent work and inclusive economic growth. Through ILO technical assistance, employers&#x2019; organizations will establish policies and programmes informed by consultations, research, and member-driven needs. This initiative will initially ascertain the needs of members and thereafter explore how employers&#x2019; organizations could respond to the emerging needs. The programme also supports employers&#x2019; organizations in developing strategic and membership plans to enhance governance, representation, performance, and sustainability. By building knowledge and promoting active engagement in social dialogue, the initiative seeks to improve the participation of employers in policy formulation and strengthen tripartite collaboration. Training will be provided to representatives and employees of member organizations on the importance, rules, and benefits of social dialogue to facilitate their meaningful participation in tripartite mechanisms. Implemented in a challenging context marked by political instability, security risks, restricted civic space, and social barriers, especially affecting women and vulnerable groups, this intervention focuses on fostering organizational resilience and inclusive engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
